SECTION 1 — MEILISEARCH TLS FLAG CONTRACT: VERIFIED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STATUS: VERIFIED. The inherited claim in `ROADMAP.md:164` / `ROADMAP.md:211`
("ship `--ssl-cert-path` / `--ssl-key-path` matching Meilisearch flag names",
carried as an explicitly UNVERIFIED claim) is now confirmed correct against
upstream. No near-miss spelling correction is needed.

No Meilisearch binary is installed on this host, so `meilisearch --help` could
not be used:

    $ which meilisearch
    meilisearch not found
    $ ls /usr/local/bin/meilisearch /opt/homebrew/bin/meilisearch
    ls: /opt/homebrew/bin/meilisearch: No such file or directory
    ls: /usr/local/bin/meilisearch: No such file or directory

Verified instead against THREE independent authoritative sources, two of which
are upstream source artifacts rather than prose documentation.

SOURCE A — Meilisearch published configuration reference (the exact URL named in
the Stage 1 checklist):
    https://www.meilisearch.com/docs/resources/self_hosting/configuration/reference
  Reported verbatim:
    --ssl-cert-path        env MEILI_SSL_CERT_PATH   "Value must be a path to
                                                      PEM-formatted certificates"
    --ssl-key-path         env MEILI_SSL_KEY_PATH    "RSA private key or PKCS8-
                                                      encoded private key, both
                                                      in PEM format"
    --ssl-auth-path        env MEILI_SSL_AUTH_PATH
    --ssl-ocsp-path        env MEILI_SSL_OCSP_PATH
    --ssl-require-auth     env MEILI_SSL_REQUIRE_AUTH
    --ssl-resumption       env MEILI_SSL_RESUMPTION
    --ssl-tickets          env MEILI_SSL_TICKETS

SOURCE B — upstream clap definitions (primary source of truth for the CLI):
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/main/crates/meilisearch/src/option.rs
  Verbatim:
    #[clap(long, env = MEILI_SSL_CERT_PATH, value_parser)]
    pub ssl_cert_path: Option<PathBuf>,

    #[clap(long, env = MEILI_SSL_KEY_PATH, value_parser)]
    pub ssl_key_path: Option<PathBuf>,

  clap's `long` derive kebab-cases the field name, so `ssl_cert_path` ->
  `--ssl-cert-path` and `ssl_key_path` -> `--ssl-key-path`. This is the
  mechanism that makes Source A's spelling authoritative rather than editorial.

SOURCE C — upstream shipped config file:
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/main/config.toml
  Verbatim:
    # Sets the server's SSL certificates.
    # ssl_cert_path = "./path/to/certfile"
    # Sets the server's SSL key files.
    # ssl_key_path = "./path/to/private-key"

CONCLUSION FOR STAGE 2 — use these exact spellings in
`engine/flapjack-server/src/main.rs`:

    --ssl-cert-path   (PEM certificate chain; first cert certifies the key,
                       last cert is a root CA)
    --ssl-key-path    (RSA or PKCS8 private key, PEM)

ENV VAR NAMING — DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE. Do NOT copy `MEILI_SSL_CERT_PATH` /
`MEILI_SSL_KEY_PATH`. Every other flag in `struct Cli`
(`engine/flapjack-server/src/main.rs:24-41`) uses the `FLAPJACK_` prefix
(`FLAPJACK_DATA_DIR`, `FLAPJACK_BIND_ADDR`, `FLAPJACK_PORT`). Stage 2 should use
`FLAPJACK_SSL_CERT_PATH` / `FLAPJACK_SSL_KEY_PATH`. The compatibility promise in
`ROADMAP.md` is about the CLI flag names an operator types; adopting a foreign
env prefix would break this repo's single env-naming convention and collide
conceptually with the existing `FLAPJACK_SSL_EMAIL` / `FLAPJACK_ACME_DIRECTORY`
owned by `engine/flapjack-ssl/src/config.rs`.

OUT OF SCOPE (recorded so a later lane does not re-verify): `--ssl-auth-path`,
`--ssl-ocsp-path`, `--ssl-require-auth`, `--ssl-resumption`, `--ssl-tickets`
exist upstream but are not in this lane's `ROADMAP.md` row.

