SECTION 5 — OPEN QUESTIONS CARRIED TO LATER STAGES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Q1 (Stage 2) — Bad-input failure mode. The `ROADMAP.md` row and the stage text
   require failing loudly rather than falling back to plaintext. Unresolved
   detail: cert/key files are read at bind time, so an unreadable or malformed
   PEM must abort startup with a nonzero exit BEFORE `print_startup_banner`
   prints a URL. Decide whether that error exits from `resolve_tls_config()` in
   `main.rs` (pure, testable, but cannot catch a file deleted between parse and
   bind) or from `serve()`. Recommendation: validate-and-load in `main.rs`,
   surface I/O errors there, and treat a later bind-time failure as a hard
   `Err` out of `serve()`.

Q2 (Stage 2/3) — Does the dashboard/swagger-ui asset path or any CORS default
   assume `http://`? `cors_origins_from_env()` defaults to loopback-only mode.
   Not traced this stage; flagged because an HTTPS origin is a different origin
   than the same host over HTTP.

Q3 (Stage 3) — Cert generation for the probe. `rcgen` 0.13 is already a
   `flapjack-ssl` dependency and could generate the self-signed pair in-process,
   avoiding a hard dependency on the host's `openssl req`. Not decided here.

Q4 (Stage 4) — Whether to fix or gap-spec the ACME path, given the discarded
   private key, the hardcoded `/etc/letsencrypt/live` path, and the
   `systemctl reload nginx` call documented in 3.3. Evidence is captured; the
   disposition is Stage 4's to make.

